## Windows platform detection in `deleteIfExists`

Based only on the content above, **`deleteIfExists` does not itself detect the Windows platform.** It handles errors in a cross-platform way by comparing the error code against both `kSystemCodeCannotFindFile` and `kSystemCodePathNotFound`, without any `platform.isWindows` check.

Windows-specific detection appears elsewhere in the file—for example, `_onFileSystemException` and `_getWindowsRetryDelay` use `platform.isWindows`—but that logic is not part of `deleteIfExists`, which is a static method with no `Platform` reference.

